    "partisan_doctrine_rule": {
        "code": "print(\"The Partisan Doctrine Rule is a trading strategy that emphasizes following the market's dominant trend. It involves buying assets during bullish trends and selling during bearish trends, with the core principle being to align trades with the prevailing market direction. The rule typically involves using momentum indicators or trend-following methods to identify and sustain trades in the direction of the market's momentum.\")",
